\begin{aligned} 527 \div 4 &= 131 \text{ remainder } 3 \\ 131 \div 4 &= 32 \text{ remainder } 3 \\ 32 \div 4 &= 8 \text{ remainder } 0 \\ 8 \div 4 &= 2 \text{ remainder } 0 \\ 2 \div 4 &= 0 \text{ remainder } 2 \end{aligned}
\] So, the base 4 representation of $527_{10}$ is $20033_4$. Now, let's find the sum of the digits: $2 + 0 + 0 + 3 + 3 = 8$. The sum of the digits in base 4 is $8_{10}$. </think> <answer> $\boxed{8}$ </answer>

